{
 "_about": "Where each history in data/prices that Yahoo no longer serves came from (former Nasdaq-100 members), how it was assembled and the checks it passed. Method: each source is read into the repo's schema; only continuous stretches that overlap the index membership with a median dollar volume of $2M or more are used (a reused symbol is another company); sources must agree on 90% of overlapping days' total returns within 2%; the base is the source with dividends and the best cover, older and newer sources are joined on overlapping days by price ratio; split events come from every source whose prices agree that day; dividends are derived from the adjusted close; days where one source moves over 30% and another under 15% take the consensus. The data job never replaces these files with a Yahoo download (a reused symbol may now be another company). Former companies of reused symbols are stored as <SYMBOL>-<YEAR> (backtester/data.py FORMER_LISTINGS).",
 "_sources": {
  "bdi": {
   "url": "https://github.com/bdi2357/DirectIndexing/tree/main/data/PriceVolume",
